[gd_resource type="ShaderMaterial" load_steps=8 format=3]

; M_FloorPlate (PBR) — the reflective floor, and still the biggest single
; win in the kit.
;
; Two wear systems overlap here and they are deliberately at different scales.
; The BAKED one is in the ORM: the tread tips are buffed, the joints hold dirt.
; The PLACED one is traffic_amount in the shader, driven by the world-space
; macro field, so a corridor develops a polished path down its middle that
; continues across module boundaries because the noise does not know where the
; modules are.
;
; wet_amount stays high. Paired with SSR and a room ReflectionProbe, a wet patch
; is free light — it doubles the apparent brightness of a room without adding a
; lumen, which is the only honest way to make a darkness-law game readable.

[ext_resource type="Shader" path="res://src/shaders/nv_surface_pbr.gdshader" id="1"]
